{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1197026-corpus-question","id":1197026,"title":"Corpus question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-18T21:24:30-07:00","id":1197026,"title":"Corpus question","content":"The Health of a spirit is Size + Resistance.<br /> <br /> Quite easy to understand. <br /> <br /> However, how do we determine the size of... a rank 3... war, or combat spirit... ?<br /> <br /> A rank 2 car spirit, or a rank 3 truck spirit are easy... but for things that are... conceptual... how do we determine the size ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2986-warriorshaman","name":"Warriorshaman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T21:34:22-07:00","id":1197027,"title":"","content":"The book explicitly provides &quot;use Rank as Size&quot; as a go-to metric for spirits of abstract concepts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T21:39:39-07:00","id":1197030,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the answer. Must have missed that part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2986-warriorshaman","name":"Warriorshaman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T05:27:12-07:00","id":1197136,"title":"","content":"But really, you can asign any Size that makes sense, spirits of about human range in Size (4-6) are usual as are those of great Rank (4+) that can tower over their lessers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T13:07:42-07:00","id":1197301,"title":"","content":"Yeah... I was assuming so myself. A spirit of war. The reprsentation was a greek, spartan soldier. However, he would wear a viking helmet, wield a japanese katana, also wield a spartan spear, well, its not clear yet, but the idea is to take a big Guy, (using the merit Giant) so it would be a size 6 spirit. Then, put on him, every great cultural warrior symbolism, like a katana, and a viking helm, we may think of... and make an mixture of those.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2986-warriorshaman","name":"Warriorshaman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T13:24:15-07:00","id":1197307,"title":"","content":"While the book says Rank as Size, I recommend adding one or two points of Size to all spirits. Remember, a Rank 4 spirit with the lowest number of Attribute dots will have an average of 9 dice on all tasks <i>not</i> pertaining to their concept. That is far beyond the often assumed human average of 4 dice, and to me it feels a bit off if such spirits are generally smaller than most humans. Especially if they don't represent anything that is smaller than humans (such as many animals). On top of that I'd also grant more Size to spirits of locations. Cities, rivers, forests, even large buildings to some degree. Their concepts are <i>large </i>and extra Size also grants them more staying power (in the form of Corpus) even if they don't have much Resistance.<br /> But this is purely opinion on how to make spirits more flavourful so feel free to just disregard this post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":".  Grammar 03-19-2018, 04:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T01:17:54-07:00","id":1197516,"title":"","content":"I just make mostly abstract spirits - like emotions, ideas, etc. - roughly human looking or at least human size ( so the have Size 5 from start ). Of course, spirits of things larger than humans simply have they physical counterparts Size. And yes, adding 1 or 2 Size points for things smaller than humans is logical and somehow setting consistent.<br /> <br /> Remember also that <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/155772-princess-mononoke-as-werewolf-spirituality-story\">source material - Princess Mononoke</a> - points spirits can be <i>large</i>...<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px